9.112.e:
The draft-horse seeks an easy-rolling chariot, beguilers a joke;
the penis seeks the hairy split, the frog just seeks water.
– O drop, flow around for Indra.

10.24.e:
O Indra, drink this honeyed soma pressed in the cup;
lay down for us a foundation of wealth in thousands, o you of many goods.
– In my exhilaration I wish to acclaim you (gods).

10.25.e:
Here he is: the exhilarating, overpowering one dear to Indra grows strong;
he strengthens the thought of great Kakṣīvant, the inspired poet.
– In my exhilaration I wish to acclaim you (gods).
